? Change the module list? (y/N) yes
? Modules to run
  [ ] user.admin: Set up an admin account that logs in with an SSH key and uses sudo (arms the safety timer)
  [ ] ssh.server: Turn off root and password logins over SSH (arms the safety timer)
  [ ] firewall.inbound: Drop incoming traffic that no rule allows (arms the safety timer)
  [ ] ssh.bruteforce: Ban addresses that keep failing to log in over SSH
  [x] kernel.sysctl: Harden kernel settings (does not apply: kernel settings belong to the host inside a container)
  [ ] updates.auto: Install security updates automatically

kernel.sysctl: not applicable (kernel settings belong to the host inside a container)

Nothing to do: this server already matches.

? Save your answers to vps-ready.toml to repeat them later? (Y/n) no
Not saved. To repeat this, save these lines to a file and run `sudo vps-ready apply --profile <file>`:

schema = 1
extends = "minimal"

[modules."firewall.inbound"]
enabled = false

[modules."ssh.server"]
enabled = false

[modules."updates.auto"]
enabled = false

[modules."user.admin"]
enabled = false
